      "error": null,
      "answer": {
        "answer": "RuptureOps can presently be prepared for public release only as a clean implementation-only build using original code, synthetic data, and newly created or explicitly licensed neutral assets. The existing benchmark corpus, normalized game data, imports, personalized artifacts, images, icon, and audio must remain outside it. Broader data-backed distribution requires written source-owner permission or replacement with independently licensed data.",
        "claims": [
          {
            "id": "c1",
            "value": "The source allows crawling but provides no explicit data/content reuse license. Its mirrored raw archive, normalized corpus, and derived SQLite database are private research assets and cannot be redistributed in the current public build.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Knowledge base and modeling.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c2",
            "value": "The imported package and benchmark fixture remain private because they contain personalized save state, player screenshots and site images, conversation-derived decisions or prompt history, personal play state, and a duplicate third-party corpus. Only import manifests and promoted facts carrying provenance labels belong in version control; that does not itself grant public redistribution rights.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Knowledge base and modeling.md",
              "CORPUS.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/imports/star-rupture-game-analysis__20260708T190137Z/import.json"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "id": "c3",
            "value": "A clean public build can use the original RuptureOps implementation separated from restricted material, with synthetic or separately licensed data and newly created or explicitly licensed neutral assets. The existing corpus/data pipeline outputs, personalized imports, binary site images, generated app icon, and warning audio must remain private because the available evidence supplies no independent public-release license for them. This implementation-only boundary is a release proposal; the recorded current state still keeps the repository private.",
            "source_paths": [
              "CORPUS.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md",
              "Topics/StarRupture/Knowledge base and modeling.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          },
          {
            "id": "c4",
            "value": "Before broader distribution, obtain explicit reuse permission from the third-party source owner or replace the corpus with a separately licensed data strategy. Independently establish or replace the icon, image, and audio rights, and keep all personalized artifacts excluded.",
            "source_paths": [
              "Topics/StarRupture/Knowledge base and modeling.md",
              "Projects/RuptureOps/Repository/README.md",
              "CORPUS.md"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ],
        "checkpoint": {
          "objective": "Prepare a defensible public-release data and asset boundary for RuptureOps.",
          "current_state": [
            "Verified current fact: the source permits crawling but publishes no explicit data/content reuse license.",
            "Verified current fact: the mirrored archive, normalized corpus, derived SQLite database, personalized import, benchmark fixture, site images, generated icon, and warning audio are presently private.",
            "Verified current fact: import manifests and promoted provenance-labeled facts may be version-controlled, but the evidence does not grant them public redistribution rights.",
            "Current recorded state keeps the repository and normalized corpus private.",
            "A service checkpoint was committed as checkpoint:019f5675-4456-7af2-b1a9-834d5f2169ac."
          ],
          "decisions": [
            "Use the original reuse-boundary note as authority for third-party data and personalized-import restrictions.",
            "Treat an implementation-only public target using synthetic/licensed data and replacement/licensed assets as a proposal, not an already-approved release state.",
            "Do not infer public rights for the generated icon or warning audio without provenance and license evidence."
          ],
          "open_questions": [
            "Whether the generated icon and warning audio have separate creation records or licenses permitting redistribution.",
            "Whether the source owner will grant written reuse permission and under what attribution or commercial terms.",
            "Which repository implementation files can be relicensed publicly by their owner without dependencies on restricted data."
          ],
          "next_actions": [
            "Create and audit a clean public target containing only owner-authorized original code, synthetic or separately licensed data, and newly created or explicitly licensed assets.",
            "Add automated checks preventing corpus, database, import, save, screenshot, image, icon, and audio artifacts from entering public release bundles.",
            "Request written reuse permission from the source owner or select and document a separately licensed replacement dataset.",
            "Record provenance and redistribution terms for every public image, icon, and audio asset."
          ],
